      "id": "TPK-01",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "Both lattice minima force a compact set of orbit representatives",
      "anchor": "inputs-thick-compact",
      "statement": "For fixed totally complex L, rank N≥1 and c>0, one compact K inside the cone meets every GL_N(𝒪_L)-orbit of positive h satisfying λ(h),λ∨(h)≥c.",
      "hypotheses": "λ measures the unconstrained minimum over nonzero vectors of 𝒪_L^N, with the sum over infinite places taken once per place. The input transference bound has squared covering radius at most C/λ∨(h).",
      "definitions": [
        "D=10ρ and ρ=C/c.",
        "For a fixed full-rank integral B, impose q_h(v)≥c for each nonzero integral v and q_h(B_j)≤D for each column.",
        "I₀(L,N) denotes the constant in the determinant lower estimate. A bound on the absolute field norm of det A controls the finite list of integral matrices up to left multiplication by Γ."
      ],
      "equations": [
        "inputs-thick-spanning"
      ],
      "dependencies": [],
      "correspondence": "The transference estimate lets a lattice vector v approximate an appropriately scaled perpendicular to the kernel of any proposed annihilator of the short vectors. q_h(z)=4ρ and q_h(z−v)≤ρ force f(v)≠0 and q_h(v)≤10ρ by the parallelogram identity. Choose N L-independent short vectors. A determinant product bound |Norm(det A)|≤I₀(L,N)(D/c)^(N r₂) gives a finite list B up to integral left multiplication. For each B the Gram coordinates have sup norm ≤2D and recover the form by invertibility; the inequalities define a closed subset lying inside the cone by rypos.",
