    {
      "id": "TPK-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "Normalize the bump where its orbit sum reaches one, then pull back",
      "anchor": "inputs-thick-weights",
      "statement": "A smooth arithmetic-equivariant map F takes the full positive cone to forms with both minima uniformly positive. A normalized bump ψ on a compact neighborhood of K satisfies ∑γ ψ(γ⁻¹F(h))=1, with locally finite translates and finitely many relative group elements for intersecting closed supports.",
      "hypotheses": "Γ is GL_N(𝒪_L) for a fixed totally complex field and positive rank. The arithmetic map uses normalized determinant, a smooth Γ-invariant proxy for the dual minimum, and the positive primal and dual lower bounds of ret. On the thick images the orbit meets K. For the orbit sum of the bump alone, the conclusion requires the orbit to meet K.",
      "definitions": [
        "nf(h)=P(h)^(−1/(N[L:ℚ]))h where P=∏_w Re(det h_w)^mult(w).",
        "μ(h) lies between λ∨(h)/4 and 4λ∨(h). ret μ(h)=μ(h)h+Σ_j ρ(4^j μ(h))term(4^j,h), with term a smoothed average of rank-one outer products divided by (4^j)².",
        "F=(ret μ)∘nf. For b≥1 on K, b≥0 supported in K′, S(k)=Σγ b(γ⁻¹k) is locally finite on the cone and invariant. ψ=b/g(S); g is smooth, bounded below by 1/2 and the identity for S≥1."
      ],
      "equations": [
        "inputs-thick-orbit-sum"
      ],
      "dependencies": [
        "TPK-01"
      ],
      "correspondence": "Properness controls integral inverses by their finitely many possible columns on a compact. It gives both a locally fixed finite list for the orbit sum and the global finite set of relative labels when translated supports overlap. An orbit hitting K has S≥1 so its ψ-sum equals 1. At N=1 and L=ℚ(i), Γ has four elements, all fixing every Hermitian scalar. The sum is over those four labels and every pulled-back weight is exactly 1/4.",
