      "id": "TPK-03",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "A single geometric sum supplies one power of height",
      "anchor": "inputs-thick-exponent",
      "statement": "One natural exponent a=1 is admissible for all N≥1. The moving-frame derivative norm of the final partition generator is ≤N Cψ Cr Cn(1+c₀⁻¹)H(x), with H(x) the inverse product of the primal and dual minima at x⋅I. Constants may vary with L,N.",
      "hypotheses": "Relative closeness Clδ is |q_k(z)−q_h(z)|≤δ q_h(z) for every real z. The normalization and ret estimates apply when their own input relative error is ≤1/4, so the composition uses δ≤1/[4(Cn+1)]. Scalar normalization preserves the product of minima. SHt supplies c₀>0 with ht x≥c₀ at every moving frame.",
      "definitions": [
        "The common exponent a in SPU precedes N. The derivative constant need not do so.",
        "In PfGRLip the lower scale 4^lo>3λ/64 bounds the full reciprocal sum by (4/3)64/(3λ)=256/(9λ). The single-scale absolute variation of the averaged matrix is ≤C δ q_h(z)/4^j.",
        "Relative to ret(h) the factor μ(h)≥cλ∨(h) supplies the second denominator. The terms due to variations of the cutoff and μ are estimated in the same proof."
      ],
      "equations": [],
      "dependencies": [
        "TPK-02"
      ],
      "correspondence": "Combine the relative Lipschitz estimates for nf, ret and ψ. The derivative lemma tests h+t(x⋅v), giving relative error N t‖v‖ before passing to a difference quotient in the moving frame. c₀≤H absorbs the additive one. The caller sPU=sPU_of sHt_of uses this partition in sSurj_of, and SWhit turns m iterative differentiations into H^m at a=1.",
